{"version":"0.3.0","body":"/**\n * ReadCardFile - Member Initiative Program\n * Reads the FIRST worksheet of a gift card import file and returns every\n * non-blank row as TEXT exactly as Excel shows it, plus the raw values.\n *\n * Why both: a card number stored as a NUMBER with more than 15 digits is already\n * rounded inside the file (Excel shows 6.92127E+20). The flow rejects those rows\n * instead of saving a wrong card number. Raw values give the flow exact dates\n * (Excel serial numbers) and amounts.\n *\n * Called by the MIPValidateCardFile / MIPImportCards flows through\n * Excel Online (Business) > \"Run script from SharePoint library\". No parameters.\n */\nfunction main(workbook: ExcelScript.Workbook): {\n    sheet: string;\n    headers: string[];\n    rows: string[][];\n    values: (string | number | boolean)[][];\n    rowNumbers: number[];\n} {\n    const ws = workbook.getWorksheets()[0];\n    const used = ws.getUsedRange();\n    if (!used) {\n        return { sheet: ws.getName(), headers: [], rows: [], values: [], rowNumbers: [] };\n    }\n    const texts = used.getTexts();\n    const vals = used.getValues();\n    const firstRow = used.getRowIndex();          // 0-based sheet row of the header\n    const headers = texts[0].map(h => String(h).trim());\n    const rows: string[][] = [];\n    const values: (string | number | boolean)[][] = [];\n    const rowNumbers: number[] = [];\n    for (let r = 1; r < texts.length; r++) {\n        const t = texts[r].map(x => String(x).trim());\n        if (t.every(x => x === \"\")) {\n            continue;                              // tables often carry empty rows\n        }\n        rows.push(t);\n        values.push(vals[r]);\n        rowNumbers.push(firstRow + r + 1);         // the row number a person sees in Excel\n    }\n    return { sheet: ws.getName(), headers, rows, values, rowNumbers };\n}","description":"","parameterInfo":"{\"version\":1,\"originalParameterOrder\":[],\"parameterSchema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"default\":{},\"x-ms-visibility\":\"internal\"},\"returnSchema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"result\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"sheet\":{\"type\":\"string\"},\"headers\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"rows\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"string\"}}},\"values\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{}}},\"rowNumbers\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"number\"}}}}}},\"signature\":{\"comment\":\"ReadCardFile - Member Initiative Program\\nReads the FIRST worksheet of a gift card import file and returns every\\nnon-blank row as TEXT exactly as Excel shows it, plus the raw values.\\n\\nWhy both: a card number stored as a NUMBER with more than 15 digits is already\\nrounded inside the file (Excel shows 6.92127E+20). The flow rejects those rows\\ninstead of saving a wrong card number. Raw values give the flow exact dates\\n(Excel serial numbers) and amounts.\\n\\nCalled by the MIPValidateCardFile / MIPImportCards flows through\\nExcel Online (Business) > \\\"Run script from SharePoint library\\\". No parameters.\",\"parameters\":[{\"name\":\"workbook\",\"comment\":\"\"}]}}","apiInfo":"{\"variant\":\"synchronous\",\"variantVersion\":2}"}